---
import report from '../report-data.json';
import evidence from '../report-evidence.json';
import {cameraEvidence} from '../report-format-math.js';
import {median} from '../report-math.js';
import {imageAttributes} from '../responsive-images.js';
import '../campaign-actions.css';
const {base}=Astro.props;
const photo=report.posts.find(post=>post.index===3305);
const chart=report.posts.find(post=>post.index===3267);
const camera=cameraEvidence(report.posts,evidence);
const cameraGroups=[{label:'To-camera videos',rows:camera.camera},{label:'Other posts',rows:camera.others}].map(group=>({...group,value:median(group.rows.map(post=>post.reactions))}));
const maximum=Math.max(...cameraGroups.map(group=>group.value));
---
<section class="report-closing campaign-actions" id="conclusion" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title"><div class="closing-inner">
<h2 id="conclusion-title">Six actions to take next</h2>
<p class="campaign-intro">Start with the next priority mission, with resource mobilization as the objective.</p>
<ol class="mission-actions" role="list">
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Agree one campaign question before each priority mission.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: relevant donor and partner interest.</p><p>Name the partners to reach, the decision they face and the evidence the mission can provide. Use that question to plan the interviews, photographs and data to collect, and carry it through the posts and follow-up.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual mission-question"><figcaption>Example campaign question</figcaption><blockquote>Grids for development</blockquote><p>Which grid investments would allow local firms to connect, produce and grow?</p><div class="mission-audience"><span>For utilities, donors and country teams</span></div></figure>
</li>
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Replace crowded composites with one purpose per page.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: clearer understanding and more shares.</p><p>Test a document post that separates the field photograph, the data, the implication and the opportunity to work with UNDP. Give each chart one finding-led title. For Instagram, use the original photograph with one line or one key number.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual document-sequence"><figcaption>Proposed four-page document</figcaption><div class="document-pages">
<div class="document-page"><div class="document-image"><img {...imageAttributes(photo,base,{width:'110px',mobileWidth:'110px',height:150,mobileHeight:150,cap:320})} alt="Field photograph from Riad’s post archive" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><span>Photograph</span></div>
<div class="document-page"><div class="document-image document-chart"><img {...imageAttributes(chart,base,{width:'110px',mobileWidth:'110px',height:150,mobileHeight:150,cap:320})} alt="Data visualization from Riad’s post archive" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><span>Evidence</span></div>
<div class="document-page"><div class="document-message">What does this change?</div><span>Implication</span></div>
<div class="document-page"><div class="document-message">Where can UNDP help?</div><span>Opportunity</span></div>
</div></figure>
</li>
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Record four short explanations directly to camera.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: more engagement and discovery.</p><p>Explain one decision or trade-off per clip, in Riad’s own words. Record alongside field visits and technical discussions; reuse the footage as short, subtitled Instagram Reels. The nine identified clips provide a promising small sample for a larger test.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual camera-comparison"><figcaption>Median reactions · March–June 2026</figcaption>
{cameraGroups.map(group=><div class="action-bar-row"><div><span>{group.label} <small>({group.rows.length})</small></span><strong>{group.value}</strong></div><div class="action-bar-track"><span style={`width:${group.value/maximum*100}%`}></span></div></div>)}
<p class="action-visual-note">Posts published in the same months</p></figure>
</li>
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Replace routine event invitations with findings people can discuss.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: substantive comments and peer referrals.</p><p>After each priority event, publish the consequential finding or disagreement and Riad’s assessment. Ask a question that a specific professional audience can answer. Invite relevant contributors to add evidence, and retain invitations when readers can actually participate.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual event-rewrite"><figcaption>Example change in emphasis</figcaption><p class="event-before">“We joined a panel on grid investment.”</p><span class="rewrite-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span><blockquote>“Which grid investment would remove the biggest constraint for local firms?”</blockquote><p class="action-visual-note">Lead with the event’s evidence, then open the discussion.</p></figure>
</li>
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Publish the evidence and UNDP’s offer on one useful web page.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: search visibility and qualified enquiries.</p><p>For each priority campaign, create or update a UNDP page with the methodology or tool, a country example and a clear contact. Use a descriptive title and dated sources. Direct interested readers there from posts and tailored emails, with a specific reason to get in touch.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual campaign-page"><figcaption>Example campaign page</figcaption><div class="campaign-page-sheet"><span class="page-domain">undp.org</span><h4>Grid investment for productive use</h4><div class="page-contents"><span>Country evidence</span><span>Methodology and tools</span><span>Technical support available</span></div><p>Discuss a country application with UNDP <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></p></div></figure>
</li>
<li>
<span class="action-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
<div class="action-copy"><h3>Turn relevant interest into a targeted technical briefing.</h3><p class="action-outcome">Target: partner requests and resource mobilization.</p><p>Select donors, country teams and delivery partners with a defined need. Follow up with a tailored note and a focused JET methodology session or digital-tool demonstration. Agree an application, a responsible colleague and the next discussion; track technical-support requests and donor conversations.</p></div>
<figure class="action-visual partner-path"><figcaption>Example follow-up</figcaption><div><span>Country team</span><p>A defined transition-planning need</p></div><div><span>Technical session</span><p>JET methodology applied to that need</p></div><div><span>Agreed next step</span><p>A country application and named lead</p></div></figure>
</li>
</ol>
</div></section>
